title: Loop_DayOpening
---
Narrator: A new day begins. Prince has a little time before evening.
Narrator: Today contains {LoopDecisionsPerDay()} decision opportunities.
<<loop_sequence_complete>>
===

title: Loop_DayOpening_A1_D1
---
Narrator: Act One, Day One.
Prince: Munir said I could return. Maybe I should hear him out.
Narrator: Prince has {LoopDecisionsPerDay()} choices to make today.
<<loop_sequence_complete>>
===

title: Loop_DayOpening_A1_D2
---
Narrator: Act One, Day Two.
Prince: Yesterday gave me more to think about than I expected.
<<loop_sequence_complete>>
===

title: Loop_DayOpening_A2_D1
---
Narrator: Act Two, Day One.
Prince: Asking a question is easy. Living with the answer is harder.
<<loop_sequence_complete>>
===

title: Loop_DayOpening_A2_D2
---
Narrator: Act Two, Day Two.
Prince: One more day. I should decide what I will carry forward.
<<loop_sequence_complete>>
===

title: Loop_Decision
---
Narrator: Decision {loop_decision_number()} of {LoopDecisionsPerDay()}.
What should Prince do?
-> Talk to Munir
    <<loop_choose_talk "Munir">>
-> Ponder
    <<loop_choose_action "Ponder">>
===

title: Loop_Talk_Munir
---
<<StartConversation "Munir">>
<<SetShot "Wide">>
Prince: Peace be upon you, Munir.
Munir: And upon you peace, Prince. What is on your mind?

-> Ask how to carry responsibility <<if HasConversationTopic("Munir", "PlayerToCharacter", "PrototypeAskAboutResponsibility")>>
    <<SetShot "CloseUp_A">>
    Prince: How do you carry people who depend on you without crushing yourself?
    <<SetShot "CloseUp_B">>
    Munir: First, notice that responsibility is not the same as control.
    Munir: Sit with that difference before you promise everyone an answer.
    <<MarkConversationTopicDiscussed "Munir" "PlayerToCharacter" "PrototypeAskAboutResponsibility">>
    <<UnlockPonderTopic "PrototypePonderResponsibility">>
    <<ChangeRelationship "Munir" 1>>
-> Ask the deeper question <<if HasConversationTopic("Munir", "PlayerToCharacter", "PrototypeAskAboutLeadership")>>
    <<SetShot "CloseUp_A">>
    Prince: Maybe leading them means admitting I cannot choose for them.
    <<SetShot "CloseUp_B">>
    Munir: That is a harder kind of courage. Guidance leaves room for another person to walk.
    <<MarkConversationTopicDiscussed "Munir" "PlayerToCharacter" "PrototypeAskAboutLeadership">>
    <<ChangeRelationship "Munir" 2>>
-> Let Munir ask something <<if HasConversationTopic("Munir", "CharacterToPlayer", "PrototypeMunirQuestion")>>
    <<SetShot "CloseUp_B">>
    Munir: When you imagine failing them, what are you truly afraid they will see?
    <<SetShot "CloseUp_A">>
    Prince: That I was never strong enough to keep the promises I made.
    <<MarkConversationTopicDiscussed "Munir" "CharacterToPlayer" "PrototypeMunirQuestion">>
    <<UnlockPonderTopic "PrototypePonderPromises">>
    <<ChangeRelationship "Munir" 1>>
-> Browse other available topics <<if HasTopicsForCurrentActor("PlayerToCharacter")>>
    <<jump TopicHub>>
-> Invite Munir to choose another topic <<if HasTopicsForCurrentActor("CharacterToPlayer")>>
    <<jump PrepareTopicHubNPC>>
-> Finish the conversation
    Prince: That is enough for today.

<<SetShot "TwoShot">>
Munir: Return when the next question becomes honest.
<<EndConversation>>
<<loop_action_complete>>
===

title: Loop_Ponder
---
<<StartPonder>>
<<SetShot "Wide">>
Prince: I should make room for one thought before I move again.

-> Sit with Munir's distinction <<if HasPonderTopic("PrototypePonderResponsibility")>>
    Prince: Responsibility asks me to act. Control asks everyone else to obey.
    Prince: Maybe I have been treating fear like proof that I must decide everything.
    <<MarkPonderTopicDiscussed "PrototypePonderResponsibility">>
    <<UnlockConversationTopic "Munir" "PlayerToCharacter" "PrototypeAskAboutLeadership">>
    <<UnlockConversationTopic "Munir" "CharacterToPlayer" "PrototypeMunirQuestion">>
-> Think about promises <<if HasPonderTopic("PrototypePonderPromises")>>
    Prince: A promise can guide me without becoming a chain around everyone I love.
    <<MarkPonderTopicDiscussed "PrototypePonderPromises">>
-> Take a quiet moment <<if HasPonderTopic("PrototypeQuietMoment")>>
    Prince: Silence does not solve anything, but it lets me hear which thought is shouting.
    <<MarkPonderTopicDiscussed "PrototypeQuietMoment">>
-> Browse other available thoughts <<if HasPonderTopics()>>
    <<jump Ponder_TopicHub>>
-> Stop pondering
    Prince: I have enough to carry back into the day.

<<EndPonder>>
<<loop_action_complete>>
===


